.TH "SCCFM-CLI INVENTORY DEVICES ASA ONBOARD" "1" "2026-08-19" "0.39.3" "sccfm-cli inventory devices asa onboard Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-inventory\-devices\-asa\-onboard \- Onboard an ASA device to SCC Firewall...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli inventory devices asa onboard
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Onboard an ASA device to SCC Firewall Manager.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fP TEXT
Human-readable name for the ASA device.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-device\-address\fP TEXT
Device address in the form host:port.
.TP
\fB\-\-username\fP TEXT
Username used to authenticate with the device.
.TP
\fB\-\-password\fP TEXT
Password used to authenticate with the device.
.TP
\fB\-\-connector\-type\fP [SDC|CDG]
Connector type used to communicate with the device.
.TP
\fB\-\-connector\-name\fP TEXT
Name of the Secure Device Connector (SDC) to use (required when connector-type is SDC).
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-certificate\fP
Skip certificate validation when onboarding.
.TP
\fB\-\-grouped\-labels\fP TEXT
Grouped labels in JSON format, e.g., '{"environment": ["prod", "us-west"]}
.TP
\fB\-\-ungrouped\-labels\fP TEXT
Free-form labels to assign to the device (can be specified multiple times).
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fP
Run a preflight check without onboarding.
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
